{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
'Twas in the year [D]of '92, in the merry month of [G]June,[D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I left my mother and a home so dear
for the girl I [A]loved on the Greenbriar shore.[D][D][G][D][A][D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
My mother dear, [D]she came to me and said "Oh son, don't go,"[G][D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
"Don't leave your mother and a home so dear
to trust a girl [A]on the Greenbriar shore. "[D][D][G][D][A][D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
But I was young [D]and reckless, too, and I craved a reckless life,[G][D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
I left my mother with a broken heart,
and I choosed that girl to [A]be my wife.[D][D][G][D][A][D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
Her hair was dark [D]and curly, too and her loving eyes were blue,[G][D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 8}
her cheeks were like the red red rose,
the girl I [A]loved on the Greenbriar shore.[D][D][G][D][A][D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 9}
The years rolled on and [D]the months rolled by, she left me all alone,[G][D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 10}
now I remember what mother said :
Never trust a girl [A]on the Greenbriar shore.[D]
{end_of_verse}
